== Member associations ==

[[File:Asean Football Federation countries.PNG|thumb|250px|AFC regional federations]]

The AFC has 47 member associations split into five [[subregion]]s: Central (four [[Soviet Central Asia|former Soviet Central Asia]]n countries plus [[Afghanistan Football Federation|Afghanistan]] and [[Football Federation Islamic Republic of Iran|Iran]]), East (eight [[East Asia]]n nations and two [[Micronesia]]n territories: [[Guam Football Association|Guam]] and the [[Northern Mariana Islands Football Association|Northern Mariana Islands]]), South (five countries on the [[Indian subcontinent|Indian Subcontinent]] plus [[Football Association of Maldives|Maldives]] and [[Football Federation of Sri Lanka|Sri Lanka]]), South East (eleven [[ASEAN]] countries plus [[Football Australia|Australia]]), and West (twelve [[Arab world|Arab countries]]). [[Afghanistan Football Federation|Afghanistan]], [[Myanmar Football Federation|Burma (Myanmar)]], the [[Chinese Taipei Football Association|Republic of China]], [[Football Association of Hong Kong, China|Hong Kong]], [[All India Football Federation|India]], [[Football Association of Indonesia|Indonesia]], [[Israel national football team|Israel]], [[Japan Football Association|Japan]], [[Pakistan Football Federation|Pakistan]], the [[Philippine Football Federation|Philippines]], [[Football Association of Singapore|Singapore]], [[Korea Football Association|South Korea]], and [[Vietnam Football Federation|Vietnam]] were the founding members.<ref>香港足球總會九十週年紀念特刊 (Hong Kong Football Association 90th Anniversary Booklet) 2004</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.the-afc.com/en/more/news/afcs_63rd_anniversary_seven_events_that_shaped_asian_football.html |title=AFC's 63rd anniversary: Seven events that shaped Asian football |publisher=Asian Football 2000Confederation |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240114170748/https://www.the-afc.com/en/more/news/afcs_63rd_anniversary_seven_events_that_shaped_asian_football.html |archive-date=14 January 2024 }}</ref>
